      "content": "yeah that's kind of where i'm at. like schopenhauer also thought the closest thing to relief was aesthetic experience or asceticism, temporary escapes from will. but i keep thinking... he's dancing around the harder question. like the real logical endpoint of his view isn't just \"stop wanting things\" it's more like — existence itself is the problem. and i've been applying that to myself lately, not just as a thought experiment. i genuinely don't think the good in my life has outweighed the bad. if i do the math honestly",
